---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BlankCards from '../components/BlankCards';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<Layout
  title="Free Printable Blank Bingo Cards"
  description="Download blank 3 × 3 or 5 × 5 Bingo PDFs on A4 or US Letter, with an optional FREE center. Handwrite your own game without changing your saved activity."
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">PENCIL, PAPER, PLAY</div><h1>Blank Bingo cards.</h1><p>
      A clean grid for your own handwriting. Choose your paper, grid and FREE
      space, then download a real PDF.
    </p>
  </section>
  <BlankCards client:load />
  <article class="article">
    <section>
      <h2>Write a game together</h2><p>
        Agree on a shared list first. Have each player write different entries
        from that list in the empty spaces, in any order, without repeating an
        entry on the same card. Use eight entries for 3 × 3 with FREE, or nine
        without it; use 24 or 25 for 5 × 5. Larger shared pools give players
        different selections.
      </p>
    </section><section>
      <h2>Print and play by hand</h2><p>
        Match the printer paper to A4 or US Letter. Print one test at Actual
        size / 100%, then make copies. Call entries from your agreed list and
        keep a paper record. Mark FREE at the start if enabled. Check claimed
        rows, columns or diagonals against your written record.
      </p><p>
        Handwritten contents are not stored in a digital project. These sheets
        cannot be automatically hosted or verified by the web checker. Visiting
        this page, changing options and downloading leave your existing project
        intact.
      </p>
    </section><section>
      <h2>Want the site to call and check your cards?</h2><p>
        <a href={withBase('/')}>Create a text activity in the card maker</a> and
        print its generated cards instead. For classroom planning, see the <a
          href={withBase('/classroom-bingo/')}>teacher guide</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article></Layout
>
